        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Aberdeen Bestiary\n- Places: Palace of Westminster, Old Royal Library, River Thames, City of Westminster, London\n- Organizations: Aberdeen University Library, House of Commons, House of Lords, Parliament of the United Kingdom\n- Topics: illuminated manuscripts, bestiaries\n\nFacts:\n- The Aberdeen Bestiary is a 12th-century English illuminated manuscript bestiary held as MS 24 at Aberdeen University Library.\n- The Aberdeen Bestiary was first listed in 1542 in the inventory of the Old Royal Library at the Palace of Westminster.\n- The Palace of Westminster is the meeting place of the House of Commons and the House of Lords, the two houses of the Parliament of the United Kingdom.\n- The Palace of Westminster is commonly known as the Houses of Parliament after its occupants.\n- The Palace of Westminster stands on the north bank of the River Thames in the City of Westminster in central London.",
